# Someone who plays the [[cello]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2009-01-20|author=Allan Kozinn|title=Shafts of Sun in Winter From the Italian Baroque|journal=w:The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2009/01/20/arts/music/20earl.html
|passage=And the cello concerto was strikingly different on Sunday: at Weill, the ensemble included two violinists and one violist, '''cellist''', bassist and lutenist, but on Sunday four more violinists, a second violist and a harpsichordist were added to give the ripieno sections of the fast movements a heftier punch than the smaller group delivered.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021-04-28|author=Lisa Abend|title=When the Cellos Play, the Cows Come Home|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/28/arts/music/cow-concert-scandinavian-cello-school.html
|passage=Though relative newcomers to classical music, they seemed closely attuned to the eight '''cellists''' onstage, raising their heads abruptly as the piece’s languid strains gave way to rapid-fire bow strokes.}}

